  "reference_protocol": "All cases run the actual public Core file and WAL modes on a copy of a pinned-SQLite UTF-16 database. Output is compared as bytes, so invalid UTF-8 remains observable. Return codes, unchanged physical database bytes and reference integrity are checked. A valid control accompanies malformed/noncanonical input. Seventy-two cases add a second actual row to distinguish chosen aggregate values and both joined source identities; 112 cases use independent seeded malformed/valid code units. The final seed differs from development. No oracle route, candidate filter, skip or output correction is used.",
  "implementation": [
    "Typed comparison applies the original SQL affinity before comparing. Encoding-specific BINARY uses actual cached native bytes for TEXT; NOCASE/RTRIM and other storage classes keep their ordinary comparator. Scalar min/max/nullif share the typed comparator. Ordinary UTF-8 BINARY comparison has a registered identity theorem.",
    "UTF-16 concatenation joins actual operand byte strings before decoding for logical observation; the result retains those same bytes. NULL propagation and the old UTF-8 operation are retained, with a registered UTF-8 identity theorem.",
    "JOIN contexts describe each actual source rowid slot and column range. Column lookup uses those source identities before checking decoded-value equality, so nullable/other-source rows cannot inherit an unrelated representation. Windows receive the same actual snapshot cache.",
    "MIN/MAX retain the chosen input ScalarValue beside the existing logical extreme and subtype. Step inputs, deferred ordering, finalized results and scalar result lookup carry its encoding/bytes. The existing first-minimum/maximum laws now additionally specify the newly introduced extremeScalar field; their logical extreme/subtype conclusions and full update equality are retained. Result.scalar_value independently proves that representation cannot change the logical result/error.",
    "Scalar query output exposes all actual typed result rows, alongside its existing ordinary result and first typed value. UTF-16 private materialization uses that output, rebases cached bytes onto the actually assigned private table/rowid/column, and verifies equality to the actual inserted cell before retaining the representation. A width/count mismatch fails instead of pairing unrelated results."
  ],
  "proof_scope": "Registered ordinary BINARY and UTF-8 concatenation identities, unchanged universally quantified logical column lookup preservation, logical aggregate-result preservation and extended exact min/max first-input update laws. The original exact production/reference record IO theorem remains. No whole-engine equivalence or complete malformed-Unicode theorem is claimed.",
  "feature_probe_scope": "The separate unit and survey each cover 88 named feature/mode cases and share their generator. Ten failures remain across trigger, WITHOUT ROWID, composite-primary-key, partial-index and expression-index families. This does not measure a global compatibility percentage.",
